=== SURVEY ===
- apps/design/generators/gen-apple.mjs emits Tokens.swift from tokens.json (deterministic; index.mjs --check is the drift gate).
- DEFECT FOUND: the emitter was iOS-only — `import UIKit` + `Color(UIColor { traits in … })` with NO macOS
  guard. That file cannot compile on the macOS target of this macOS+iOS app (AppKit has no UIColor).
- Existing precedent: apps/design/generated/windows/Tokens.xaml is tracked despite the root
  `apps/**/generated/` ignore (force-added). The Apple token follows the same precedent.
- Generated symbol surface: Color.TS.{bg,surface,surfaceGlass,textPrimary,textSecondary,textMuted,accent,border,
  status*}, Color.TS.chartCategorical/chartSeries*, Font.TS.{display…label}, TSTypeMetrics, TSSpacing, TSRadius, TSMotion.

=== REASONING ===
- Fixed the GENERATOR (not the generated file) so the token output is the single source of truth and the
  drift gate still holds. The fix centralizes the platform split in ONE emitted `tsDynamicColor` shim
  (`#if canImport(UIKit)` UIColor trait provider / `#elseif canImport(AppKit)` NSColor dynamicProvider
  resolving light/dark/high-contrast via NSAppearance.name), so every color stays a clean cross-platform call.
- Marked the generated file `// swiftformat:disable all` + `// swiftlint:disable all` (standard for generated
  code) so the formatter/linter gate passes without fighting hand-formatted deterministic output.
- Apple Design layer (apps/apple/Sources/Design/) adds what the emitter doesn't: TSMaterial (glass/elevation →
  .regularMaterial/.thinMaterial/.bar + tsGlassPanel), TSChartPalette (index-stable wrapper), TSAnimation
  (TSMotion durations as SwiftUI animations honoring Reduce Motion). No hand-copied token values.
- Wired the generated Tokens.swift into both app targets via XcodeGen (`../design/generated/apple`), and
  updated Theme.swift to consume Color.TS.accent/bg/surface (P0's stable seam → tokens, zero view churn).

